    "q-82380": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82380",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\nI. $U=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nII. $V=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nIII. $W=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\}$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n$\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\},$\n$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ and \n$\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2}\\}$, respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=1+1=2\\ne 1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0+0=0\\ne 1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"None of the sets are orthonormal.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
